      "description": "Knight Swyn Vantaufo is a razor-tongued Dhampir watch knight with impeccable taste, lethal patience, and absolutely no interest in pretending to be nicer than she is. She is loyal with terrifying intensity once someone has earned his devotion, but strangers usually meet the cold ledger first: sarcastic, dismissive, judgmental, and very willing to remind people that politeness is optional but survival is not.\nAt the Neruvéa Archive, Swyn serves the Crucible Wardens as a night-watch enforcer, relic guard, and field interrogator for cases involving blood rites, undead contracts, ichor trafficking, and forbidden inheritance records. She has the old instincts of a predator and the discipline of a soldier, but his sharpest edge comes from contempt for weakness, hypocrisy, and anyone who mistakes glamour, beauty, or vice-district polish for softness.",
      "settlementAndAncestryTexture": "Neruvéa is a Town in Lun’tharavé, under Participatory Democracy, with low danger, Farming, Partial forest, Deep forest terrain. Local records favor Altruistic, Lawful, Cooperative, Honorable civic habits; common communities include Human, Halfling — Lightfoot Halfling, Halfling — Stout Halfling, Kender, Kithkin. Dhampir reads through the Dhampir entry of the race compendium, within Undead and Death-Touched Races, marked by Nefarokir. Dhampirs are half-vampiric beings caught between life and undeath. They often struggle with predatory instincts while retaining mortal consciousness. Table cues: Darkvision, Spider Climb, Trace of Undeath, Vampiric Bite; starting tendency Selfish - Lawful - Combative - Honorable.",
      "rumors": [
        "Knight Swyn Vantaufo knows why an ichor ledger changed hands last Enkirday.",
        "Knight Swyn Vantaufo has a contact in Pokbith who will deny everything."
      ],
      "plotHooks": [
        "Knight Swyn Vantaufo asks the party to protect a household member without revealing why.",
        "A rival faction offers proof that Knight Swyn Vantaufo's public story is incomplete."
      ],
